WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.097
Say you need the longest stretch of a string with no repeated letters.

00:07.097 --> 00:14.700
The obvious way checks every start and every end: 36 windows for 8 letters.

00:15.000 --> 00:19.221
Instead, keep a window.

00:19.221 --> 00:31.700
Move its right edge one letter at a time and remember what’s inside.

00:32.000 --> 00:42.947
When a letter repeats, slide the left edge forward until the repeat is gone.

00:42.947 --> 00:47.700
The window never moves backwards.

00:48.000 --> 00:53.778
Each letter enters once and leaves once.

00:53.778 --> 00:55.944
One pass, O(n).

00:55.944 --> 00:59.700
That’s the sliding window.
